{% comment %}
  Purelane product card — the one card used by the shop grid, the combos rail and the
  bundle tiers. The brief notes that several sections render similar cards, so there is
  one implementation with a variant switch rather than three near-identical copies.

  Accepts:
    product      {Object}  required. A Shopify product.
    variant      {String}  'shop' (default) | 'combo' | 'tier'
    show_rating  {Boolean} default true
    show_badge   {Boolean} default true
    index        {Number}  position in the grid, used only to stagger the reveal
    heading_tag  {String}  h3 by default; callers set it to keep heading order sane

  Everything shown here is platform data or a metafield. Nothing is hardcoded: prices,
  savings and the discount percentage are computed from compare_at_price, so a merchant
  changing a price in admin updates the card with no developer involved.

  Edge cases handled deliberately, because the brief asks for a store seeded with them:
    - sold out            -> disabled button, card keeps its height
    - no image            -> placeholder at the same aspect ratio, never a collapsed card
    - very long title     -> clamped to two lines, full text still available to AT
    - no compare-at price -> strikethrough and discount pill are omitted, not left empty
    - no rating metafield -> rating row omitted rather than rendering "0.0"
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign variant = variant | default: 'shop'
  assign heading_tag = heading_tag | default: 'h3'
  if show_rating == nil
    assign show_rating = true
  endif
  if show_badge == nil
    assign show_badge = true
  endif

  assign rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value
  assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value
  assign badge = product.metafields.custom.badge.value

  assign on_sale = false
  if product.compare_at_price > product.price
    assign on_sale = true
    assign saving = product.compare_at_price | minus: product.price
    assign discount = saving | times: 100.0 | divided_by: product.compare_at_price | round
  endif

  assign delay_class = ''
  case index
    when 1
      assign delay_class = 'rv-d1'
    when 2
      assign delay_class = 'rv-d2'
    when 3
      assign delay_class = 'rv-d3'
  endcase
-%}

<article class="glass card rv {{ delay_class }} card--{{ variant }}">
  <a class="card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">
    <div class="shot">
      {%- if show_badge and badge != blank -%}
        <span class="pill">{{ badge }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
        {{
          product.featured_image
          | image_url: width: 600
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'lazy',
            decoding: 'async',
            widths: '200,300,400,600',
            sizes: '(min-width: 1024px) 280px, 45vw',
            alt: product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title,
            class: 'card__image'
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          No image is a real merchandising state, not an error. A fixed-ratio placeholder
          keeps the grid aligned and prevents layout shift.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="card__image card__image--empty" role="img"
              aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} — image coming soon">
          {%- render 'purelane-icon', icon: 'leaf' -%}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <{{ heading_tag }} class="card__title" title="{{ product.title | escape }}">
      {{- product.title -}}
    </{{ heading_tag }}>
  </a>

  {%- if show_rating and rating != blank -%}
    <div class="rate">
      <b aria-hidden="true">★ {{ rating.rating | round: 1 }}</b>
      <span class="visually-hidden">
        Rated {{ rating.rating | round: 1 }} out of {{ rating.scale_max }}
      </span>
      {%- if rating_count > 0 -%}
        · {{ rating_count }} {{ rating_count | pluralize: 'review', 'reviews' }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    A bare <s> around the compare-at price reads to a screen reader as two prices in a
    row with no indication which is current. The visually-hidden labels are the only
    thing separating "₹200, was ₹299" from "₹200 ₹299".
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pr">
    <span class="visually-hidden">
      {%- if on_sale -%}
        {{ 'products.product.price.sale_price' | t }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'products.product.price.regular_price' | t }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
    <strong>{{ product.price | money }}</strong>
    {%- if on_sale -%}
      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.price.regular_price' | t }}</span>
      <s>{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
      <em>{{ discount }}% off</em>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    A real form, not the prototype's decorative <button>. Posting to /cart/add means the
    card works with Dawn's cart drawer and with JavaScript disabled.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product.available -%}
    {%- form 'product', product, class: 'card__form' -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
      <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" type="submit" name="add">
        Add to cart
        <span class="visually-hidden">— {{ product.title | escape }}</span>
      </button>
    {%- endform -%}
  {%- else -%}
    <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" type="button" disabled aria-disabled="true">
      Sold out
      <span class="visually-hidden">— {{ product.title | escape }}</span>
    </button>
  {%- endif -%}
</article>
